(  Did you find any vulnerabilities in the contract?) Tj T*
(    No audit happened, so "found" is the wrong word. But HZ-001, HZ-005 and HZ-009 are not shapes: the) Tj T*
(    behaviour was reproduced against this exact contract, not a lookalike - a still-valid action is) Tj T*
(    destroyed by a permissionless trigger in the same block. That makes it a demonstrated hazard rather) Tj T*
(    than a candidate; it becomes a finding when somebody shows it is reachable, and a bug when the code) Tj T*
(    is not meant to behave that way. Nothing else matched.) Tj T*
(    seen: no matching selector, so this is its shape) Tj T*
(    not answered here: Whether anything here is reachable, and whether it is a bug rather than a) Tj T*
(    decision. Presence is not proof; absence is not clearance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  So is it safe to use?) Tj T*
(    Unknown, and this sheet will not pretend otherwise. What it can say is narrow and true: which hazard) Tj T*
(    shapes are present \(3\), which behaviours have been demonstrated \(a placard that says confirmed\), and) Tj T*
(    which classes the code does not match at all. What it cannot say is whether any of them is) Tj T*
(    reachable, whether the economics make it exploitable, or whether a hazard is a bug or a deliberate) Tj T*
(    choice - intent is not in the bytecode.) Tj T*
(    seen: no matching selector, so this is its shape) Tj T*
(    not answered here: The honest one: the state of the owner key, what you have approved, and what) Tj T*
